{
  "format": "zapterm-command-lists",
  "version": 1,
  "platform": "fortianalyzer",
  "notes": "FortiAnalyzer 7.6 command lists. Every command was checked against the FortiAnalyzer 7.6.0 CLI reference (docs.fortinet.com/document/fortianalyzer/7.6.0/cli-reference): get system, diagnose fortilogd, diagnose log, diagnose sql, diagnose report, diagnose dvm, diagnose fmnetwork, diagnose system, diagnose sniffer, execute. Read-only commands only. Left out on purpose: diagnose sql remove/rebuild, process kill, report clean, log restore cancel, fortilogd msgstat flush and every other command that deletes, rebuilds or resets. The sniffer carries a caution quoting the sniffer reference (“Packet capture can be very resource intensive”) and its count is limited to 1–1000.",
  "label": "FortiAnalyzer · 7.6",
  "stopDebug": [],
  "stopKeys": "\u0003",
  "lists": [
    {
